  "instance_name": "spiritualization_of_trauma",
  "label": "Spiritualization of Trauma",
  "description": "A conceptual framework where the psychological and emotional trauma experienced by individuals in high-stress or dangerous professions is framed as something that requires spiritual or divine intervention rather than professional psychological support or societal recognition. This can be seen as minimizing the human cost of the work and potentially implying that the only way to cope is through faith or prayer, which may be harmful by downplaying the need for mental health resources and systemic support.",
